    "graphrag": {
      "answer": "Over the 2017–2022 period, Third Party Android is projected to have the highest CAGR among all platforms, reaching 17.9%. [G27] [G70] Americas and EMEA share the highest regional CAGR at 14.3%. [G27] The 2018 worldwide app market is $146B, led by iOS at $92B (63%), followed by Google Play at $27B (19%) and Third Party Android at $26B (18%). [G27] [G7] The projected pattern therefore combines an iOS-dominated 2018 baseline with the strongest subsequent platform growth momentum shifting toward Third Party Android through 2022. [G27] [G70] [G14] The supplied evidence does not establish that Third Party Android overtakes iOS by 2022. [G27] [G70]",
